<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bisenzio</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bisenzio is a river of Tuscany that flows from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> south through Prato into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arno">Arno</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>. Its water powered fulling mills and dye works that sustained Prato's woollen cloth industry from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, a canal system still known as the gore.</p></div>
